Subject: [PATCH] rtems-esp-wifi: preserve default coexistence priorities

When coexistence is disabled, ESP-IDF returns success without changing the
priority supplied by the caller. Do not replace the C5 HAL default priority
of one with zero.

--- a/src/rtems_wifi_os_adapter.c
+++ b/src/rtems_wifi_os_adapter.c
@@ -1670,16 +1670,11 @@
 
 static int rtems_wifi_coex_pti_get( uint32_t service, uint8_t *pti )
 {
+  /* Match ESP-IDF with coexistence disabled: retain the caller's defaults.
+   * In particular, C5 initializes its default arbitration priority to one.
+   */
   (void) service;
-
-  /*
-   * Packet traffic arbitration priority.  With no competing radio every
-   * request wins, and zero is the value ESP-IDF's own stub returns when
-   * coexistence is compiled out.
-   */
-  if ( pti != NULL ) {
-    *pti = 0;
-  }
+  (void) pti;
 
   return 0;
 }
